course: dictionary
lesson: 12267
title: Contingent: depends on something else
level: primary-6
stars: 2
explain: «Contingent» is a long, formal word. Its most common meaning is depending on something else. If A is contingent on B, A only happens if B happens first. «The picnic is contingent on good weather» means no good weather, no picnic.
explain: The word can also mean a group. «The school sent a large contingent to the parade.» Here a contingent is a group of people who belong to a bigger group and are sent or gathered together. If the word is followed by «on» or «upon», it is probably the first meaning. If it is followed by «of», it is probably the group meaning.
explain: Sometimes it means possible but not certain: «Our plan is still contingent, because nobody knows yet.» Try the check: put «only if» into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: Contingent is a formal word, so you will meet it most often in rules, exams and the news.
fact: «Contingent on» means «only if»: «The prize is contingent on getting every answer right» means you win only if every answer is right.
fact: As a noun, «a contingent» is a group, such as «a contingent of soldiers» or «the Irish contingent».
fact: As an adjective, contingent can also mean possible but not certain, something that may or may not happen.
fact: Good tip: say «only if» in the sentence. If it fits, the first meaning is right.
exercise: «The trip is contingent on good weather.» What does contingent mean here? | Sure to happen | *Depending on something else happening first | Very cold and wet | A group of friends
exercise: «The school sent a large contingent to the parade.» What is a contingent here? | A type of cloud | *A group of people sent together | A kind of parade float
exercise: «Our plan is contingent upon the bus being on time.» Which phrase could replace contingent? | Loud | *Only if | Forgotten | Certain
test: «Our trip is contingent upon the weather.» What does contingent mean? | Very expensive | *Depends on something else | Given to everyone | Sudden
test: «The match is contingent, because it might be cancelled.» What does contingent mean here? | Very fast | Certain to happen | A group of players | *Possible but not certain
exam: Which meaning of contingent is used in «a large contingent of fans»? | *A group of people belonging to a larger group | Very loud | Depending on something else | Possible but not certain
